+# TLS Certificate Verification
+
+The project's current recorded policy is HTTPS everywhere with no plaintext exception: all communication, regardless of source, destination, or environment (development, staging, or production), must use HTTPS with TLS certificate verification enabled. This supersedes an earlier, now-retired allowance that disabled certificate verification in development builds.
